1
00:00:00,200 --> 00:00:02,200
What makes the same digit worth ten

2
00:00:02,280 --> 00:00:03,000
times as much?

3
00:00:03,360 --> 00:00:04,320
Its position does.

4
00:00:04,700 --> 00:00:07,200
In our base ten system, ten ones make

5
00:00:07,260 --> 00:00:09,540
one ten, and ten tens make one hundred.

6
00:00:10,140 --> 00:00:11,860
Each place is ten times the place

7
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:13,280
immediately to its right.

8
00:00:13,920 --> 00:00:15,360
Look at four hundred and seventy two

9
00:00:15,460 --> 00:00:17,440
thousand, six hundred and thirty one.

10
00:00:17,920 --> 00:00:20,180
Put each digit into its own column, from

11
00:00:20,220 --> 00:00:21,920
hundred thousands down to ones.

12
00:00:22,400 --> 00:00:23,860
The seven is in the ten thousands

13
00:00:23,940 --> 00:00:24,240
column.

14
00:00:24,620 --> 00:00:27,300
Its value is seventy thousand, not seven

15
00:00:27,400 --> 00:00:27,800
thousand.

16
00:00:28,560 --> 00:00:30,720
The two stands for two thousand, the six

17
00:00:30,740 --> 00:00:32,400
for six hundred, and the three for

18
00:00:32,440 --> 00:00:32,740
thirty.

19
00:00:33,220 --> 00:00:35,160
Reading the number in groups helps: four

20
00:00:35,200 --> 00:00:36,960
hundred and seventy two thousand, then

21
00:00:37,020 --> 00:00:38,160
six hundred and thirty one.

22
00:00:38,900 --> 00:00:40,080
Every digit has a job.

23
00:00:40,460 --> 00:00:42,380
Now compare the two fives in fifty five

24
00:00:42,420 --> 00:00:42,860
thousand.

25
00:00:43,200 --> 00:00:44,720
The first five represents fifty

26
00:00:44,820 --> 00:00:45,260
thousand.

27
00:00:45,560 --> 00:00:47,160
The second represents five thousand.

28
00:00:47,720 --> 00:00:49,540
Fifty thousand is ten times five

29
00:00:49,600 --> 00:00:51,620
thousand, even though the digits look

30
00:00:51,660 --> 00:00:52,160
the same.

31
00:00:52,640 --> 00:00:54,980
This relationship helps us multiply and

32
00:00:55,040 --> 00:00:56,640
divide whole numbers by ten.

33
00:00:57,340 --> 00:00:59,120
Thirty four times ten is three hundred

34
00:00:59,160 --> 00:00:59,580
and forty.

35
00:00:59,980 --> 00:01:02,180
Each digit takes a place worth ten times

36
00:01:02,240 --> 00:01:02,660
as much.

37
00:01:03,060 --> 00:01:04,800
Three hundred and forty divided by ten

38
00:01:05,220 --> 00:01:06,280
returns thirty four.

39
00:01:06,920 --> 00:01:09,280
Try the page example: five hundred and

40
00:01:09,320 --> 00:01:11,280
eighty three thousand, two hundred and

41
00:01:11,380 --> 00:01:11,880
fourteen.

42
00:01:12,260 --> 00:01:13,960
The eight is in the ten thousands place,

43
00:01:14,020 --> 00:01:15,540
so it represents eighty thousand.

44
00:01:16,240 --> 00:01:18,840
Remember: name the place first, then

45
00:01:18,900 --> 00:01:19,700
work out the value.

46
00:01:20,140 --> 00:01:22,080
One place left means ten times as much.
